Lets the core take a link dragged over a page while it's over the targets of the app's split
view, so a link let go there opens in a pane beside the page (issue #694). Blink won't take a link
dropped on its own page, and WebDragDestDelegate is told of a drag with no point and can't take
it. The drag destinations, the Mac's and Aura's, ask content::HandlePageLinkDrag at each update,
as the drag leaves and at the drop. Over the targets, the drag is the core's: the page is left and
sees no drop, and once the drag is off them again the next update enters the page again. A hook
only: the core decides where, through content::SetPageLinkDragHandler.

